    <note id="bBT">
      <content>
        <p>This is the system working today. From one sentence each, the engine produced four different genres: a platformer, two top-down games, and a tower defense. The art, the layout, the camera, and the core gameplay loop are all generated, not assembled from a fixed template. Each one is a genuinely playable game, with a documented mechanic spec and a downloadable build. The point for investors is twofold: the generation is real and genre-agnostic, and the same engine that produces these worlds is the engine that runs our forecasts. The playable surface proves the world underneath is coherent. We are not showing a concept; we are showing working worlds.</p>
      </content>
